.TH tkuxdo n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkuxdo
.PP
Real keyboard and mouse input for end\-to\-end tests of a Tk application, sent through the X server with \fBxdotool\fR (XTEST). Focus, the keyboard map, key bindings, menu traversal and pointer clicks behave as for a user. Meant for an X display of its own without a window manager, usually Xvfb. On a desktop the input would go to whichever window has the focus, and \fBsetup\fR would change the keyboard map; so \fBavailable\fR is 0 when a window manager runs (\fBunavailable\fR says why), unless \fBTKUXDO_DESKTOP=1\fR is set:
.CS
xvfb-run -a wish tests/xdo.test
.CE
.CS
package require tkutils::tkuxdo
set X ::tkutils::tkuxdo
if {![${X}::available]} { … skip … }
${X}::setup -layout de                 ;# keys for ä ö ü ß €
${X}::focusWindow .
${X}::key ctrl+n                       ;# application shortcut
${X}::type {Grüße, 1.000,50 €}
${X}::key Tab shift+Tab Return Escape
${X}::click .buttons.primary
${X}::click .main.list -double 1 -x 40 -y 12
${X}::menuSelect . "Beleg/Zahlung erfassen…"   ;# F10, Right/Down, Return
${X}::choose .form.kunde {K1 – Müller}  ;# readonly combobox by keyboard
${X}::focusWidget .form.menge          ;# X focus to the window, Tk focus to w
.CE
.PP
\fBmenuSelect\fR counts like Tk's keyboard traversal: separators and disabled entries are skipped; a disabled target is an error. If an earlier entry ran a modal dialog and left the focus on the menu bar, it is moved back first.
.PP
\fBchoose combo value\fR opens the list with \fBDown\fR, waits until it is mapped, moves to the value with \fBDown\fR/\fBUp\fR, takes it with \fBReturn\fR and waits until the list is closed. A pointer click on a readonly combobox opens or closes the list depending on its state, and keys pressed before the list is mapped go elsewhere; \fBchoose\fR avoids both.
.PP
Modal dialogs: \fBdialog\fR hands a list of steps to \fBtkutils::tkutest::answer\fR; they run once the dialog is mapped and focused:
.CS
set t [${X}::dialog -title "Neue Position" {{type Schrauben} {key Tab} {type 1,5} {key Return}}]
fa::posNeu
::tkutils::tkutest::result $t
.CE
.PP
\fBclickButton label\fR inside the steps clicks a button of that dialog with the pointer (by label or path tail), \fBchooseField name value\fR chooses in a combobox field of a tkuform dialog, \fBclickField name\fR clicks into a field of the dialog. A readonly combobox opens with \fBDown\fR, moves with \fBDown\fR/\fBUp\fR and takes the choice with \fBReturn\fR; a checkbutton toggles with \fBspace\fR.
.PP
Every command waits for the X server and then processes Tk events, so the next line of the test sees the effect. \fBfocusWindow\fR and \fBmenuSelect\fR avoid Tk's \fBfocus\fR and \fBmenu\fR; \fBtype\fR, \fBkey\fR and \fBclick\fR share their names with tkutest, so import only one of the two namespaces.
.SS Commands
.TS
l l.
command	does
\fBavailable\fR, \fBunavailable\fR	1 if usable; else why not (\fB""\fR if usable)
\fBwindowManager\fR	1 if a window manager runs on the display
\fBsetup ?\-layout xkb?\fR	check the display, set the keyboard map (\fBsetxkbmap\fR)
\fBfocusWindow top\fR	give \fBtop\fR the X focus
\fBfocusWidget w\fR	X focus to the toplevel of \fBw\fR, Tk focus to \fBw\fR
\fBtype text ?\-delay ms?\fR	type \fBtext\fR through the X server
\fBkey keysym ...\fR	press keys one after another (\fBctrl+s\fR, \fBTab\fR, \fBReturn\fR)
\fBclick w ?\-x? ?\-y? ?\-button n? ?\-double 0/1?\fR	move the pointer to \fBw\fR and click
\fBmenuSelect top path\fR	choose a menu entry by keyboard (F10, Right/Down, Return)
\fBchoose combo value\fR	choose in a readonly combobox by keyboard
\fBdialog ?\-title glob? ?\-timeout ms? steps\fR	answer the next dialog with steps, returns a token
\fBclickButton label ?top?\fR	click a button of the dialog (or of \fBtop\fR)
\fBchooseField name value\fR, \fBclickField name\fR	dialog steps for fields of a tkuform dialog
\fBpump ?ms?\fR	process Tk events for \fBms\fR (default 150)
.TE
.PP
A step in \fBdialog\fR is a command of this namespace with its arguments, e.g. \fB{type Schrauben}\fR or \fB{clickButton OK}\fR.
.PP
Errors: \fB{TKUTILS TKUXDO <REASON>}\fR (DISPLAY, LAYOUT, XDOTOOL, MENU, VALUE, USAGE, OPTION). X11 only; elsewhere \fBavailable\fR is 0. Not in the umbrella.
